{"title":"Visit Al Noor","sub":"How can a Gulf state double its international tourists?","type":"Public sector","industry":"Tourism / government","geo":"Gulf region (fictional state)","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"35 min","skills":"Growth maths · capacity constraints · stakeholders","prompt":"The tourism authority of Al Noor, a (fictional) Gulf state, receives 5 million international visitors a year. As part of its plan to diversify the economy away from oil, the government wants 10 million visitors a year by 2033 (7 years from now). The minister has asked us what it would take.","clarify":[{"q":"Why tourism?","a":"Jobs for nationals, foreign currency, less dependence on oil revenue."},{"q":"Where do visitors come from?","a":"GCC neighbours 40%, Europe 25%, South Asia 20%, others 15%."},{"q":"Hotels?","a":"35,000 hotel rooms, ~70% occupancy. 80% of visitors stay in hotels for 4 nights on average, 1.8 guests per room."},{"q":"Pipeline?","a":"12,000 rooms under construction or approved."}],"structure":{"root":"What does it take to reach 10M visitors?","branches":[{"head":"Demand","items":["Source markets & growth","Reasons to visit: attractions, events","Marketing, visas, price"]},{"head":"Access","items":["Flights & seat capacity","Airport capacity","Visa process"]},{"head":"Capacity","items":["Hotel rooms","Holiday homes","Workforce"]},{"head":"Delivery","items":["Public vs private roles","Funding & incentives","Sustainability"]}]},"hypothesis":"Doubling in 7 years needs ~10% growth a year. That's hard but doable. I suspect hotel capacity and flights, not demand, will be the bottleneck.","questions":[{"q":"What annual growth rate is needed?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>(10 ÷ 5)^(1/7) − 1 ≈ <b>10.4% a year</b>. Rule of 72 check: 72 ÷ 10.4 ≈ 7 years to double. ✓</p>"},{"q":"How many hotel rooms will Al Noor need for 10M visitors? Assume a healthy target occupancy of 75%.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Guest-nights = 10M × 80% × 4 = 32M → room-nights = 32M ÷ 1.8 ≈ <b>17.8M</b>.</p> <p>Rooms = 17.8M ÷ (365 × 75%) ≈ <b>65,000 rooms</b>. Today 35,000 + 12,000 pipeline = 47,000 → shortfall ≈ <b>18,000 rooms</b>.</p> <p>Sanity check on today: 5M × 0.8 × 4 ÷ 1.8 ≈ 8.9M room-nights ÷ (35,000 × 365) ≈ 70% occupancy. ✓ matches the data.</p>"},{"q":"Air capacity is the other constraint. What do you conclude?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"358.288281pt\" height=\"186.956pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 358.288281 186.956\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-11-06T21:01:25.472096</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.11.2, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 186.956 \nL 358.288281 186.956 \nL 358.288281 0 \nL 0 0 \nL 0 186.956 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 27.448281 161.056 \nL 351.088281 161.056 \nL 351.088281 28 \nL 27.448281 28 \nL 27.448281 161.056 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\">\n     <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n      <defs>\n       <path id=\"me79d67f2d0\" d=\"M 0 0 \nL 0 3.5 \n\" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/>\n      </defs>\n      <g>\n       <use xlink:href=\"#me79d67f2d0\" x=\"73.129525\" y=\"161.056\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/>\n      </g>\n     </g>\n     <g id=\"text_1\">\n      <!-- GCC --