xSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(105.703125 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1a\" transform=\"translate(161.203125 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(238 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-b\" transform=\"translate(273.09375 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(329.890625 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-13\" transform=\"translate(353.484375 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(411.484375 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(467.484375 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(502.171875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" transform=\"translate(557.078125 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(613.875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(648.96875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(673.96875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-f\" transform=\"translate(727.375 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(754.578125 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-70\" transform=\"translate(778.171875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" transform=\"translate(811.671875 0)\"/>\n      <use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-71\" transform=\"translate(892.875 0)\"/>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p18221b7bf9\">\n   <rect x=\"27.448281\" y=\"28\" width=\"323.64\" height=\"133.056\"/>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Visitors by source market, millions","note":"Growth potential = analyst estimate of extra visitors by 2033 with better flights and visas. Most GCC visitors arrive by road; Europe, South Asia and others arrive by air."},"answer":"<p>Potential growth totals ~5.0M, just enough for the 10M target, with <b>Europe and South Asia</b> making up ~70% of it. These are long-haul and flight-dependent: new routes and airline deals are critical. GCC visitors mostly drive, so they don't need flights.</p>"},{"q":"What should the government do, and what should it leave to the private sector?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Government:</b> e-visa / visa on arrival for priority markets; incentives for airlines on new routes; airport capacity; an events calendar; training nationals for hospitality jobs</li> <li><b>Private sector:</b> build the 18,000 extra rooms (land or tax incentives to attract them); attractions; tour operators</li> <li><b>Both:</b> sustainability standards (water, energy) and protecting the culture that attracts visitors</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Reaching 10 million visitors by 2033 needs ~10% growth a year, and the binding constraints are capacity, not demand. Al Noor needs ~65,000 hotel rooms, about 18,000 beyond today's pipeline, and new flight routes from Europe and South Asia, which offer ~70% of the growth. I recommend that government focuses on visas, airline route deals, events and a national workforce programme, and uses land and tax incentives to bring in private hotel investment. Next step: a joint plan with the national airline for 10 new routes.","great":["Converts visitors into rooms correctly","Checks the model against today's 70% occupancy","Separates public and private roles","Links tourism to the government's real goal (jobs, diversification)"],"id":10,"slug":"visit-al-noor"}